### Assessment of the change at `02a43ab20`

- **Freeze, sweep chain, and trusted-history invariants ([legacy_frozen.sh](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-legacy/src/scripts/checks/legacy_frozen.sh#L60-L204))**:
  - `chain()` verifies each transition `frozen -> sweep 1 -> ... -> HEAD:legacy`, requiring each sweep commit to be an ancestor of `HEAD` and its target to be a tree object, allowing additions only when the exact mode and blob match at that step's sweep commit and the path no longer exists at `HEAD`'s root, refusing all modifications and control-character paths, using `git diff-tree -z` and `GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS=1` so C-quoted or pathspec-magic paths cannot bypass lookups, and allowing deletions only when every covering row in `RETENTION.tsv` has `status = resolved`.
  - `lock_history()` and `history_identity()` enforce append-only lock history and path-version immutability across `main`'s trusted first-parent chain (`trusted_base`), preventing lock-row rewrites/removals and delete-then-re-add attacks with altered bytes or modes.
  - Every helper runs through `checked()`, which fails closed if a subprocess exits nonzero even when stdout is empty.
- **Single strict lock reader ([legacy_lock.py](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-legacy/src/scripts/checks/lib/legacy_lock.py#L35-L90))**:
  - Validates raw bytes before decoding (refusing empty files, NUL bytes, CR bytes, non-ASCII bytes, missing final LF, `--preview` markers, duplicate lines, missing `tree` line, wrong record kinds/field counts, non-single-space separators, and non-40/64-char lowercase hex OIDs).
  - Structural controls `named_readers()` and `lock_uses()` in [legacy_frozen.sh](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-legacy/src/scripts/checks/legacy_frozen.sh#L211-L229) verify that no other active script names or parses `legacy.lock`.
- **Swept-file link checking and fail-closed discovery ([doc_links.py](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-legacy/src/scripts/checks/lib/doc_links.py#L167-L260), [doc_links.sh](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-legacy/src/scripts/checks/doc_links.sh#L126-L190))**:
  - `swept_files()` uses `legacy_lock.load()` and checks all Markdown files in `HEAD:legacy` that were not in the frozen tree (`now - frozen`), failing closed on malformed locks, lock read errors, `ls-tree` failures, or `ls-files` failures without falling back to `rglob` when `.git` is present.
- **Sweep scope and restored dated archives ([RETENTION.tsv](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-legacy/src/RETENTION.tsv#L45-L47), [docs/decisions.md](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-legacy/src/docs/decisions.md#L201))**:
  - Sweeps only the completed records (`bugs-2026-11`, `landing-audit-2026-11-06`, `legacy_move.sh`, `move_prereqs.py`, `IDEAS.md`, `MERGED.md`), removes the duplicate root copy of `site-down.md`, and keeps the dated decision archives (`roadmap-2026-11`, `decisions-2026-11-05`, `crucial-2026-11-06`, `no-hidden-traps-2026-11-06`) at the root until `docs/decisions.md` consolidates all of their decisions and verbatim quotes, matching P21 as revised on 2026-11-08.

